// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
`verilator_config
// SEP cocotb/Verilator public-signal scope.
// (Comment lines must NOT start with the word "verilator" -- the lexer would treat
//  "// verilator ..." as a metacomment directive and fail to parse this file.)
//
// cocotb's runner forces a global --public-flat-rw, which marks every signal in the
// design public. That defeats Verilator's split_var optimisation: the split_var
// pragmas already present in the AXI fabric cells (rr_arb_tree, lzc, axi_demux) are
// silently disabled on public signals, so Verilator cannot break the false
// combinational ready/valid SCCs in axi_demux / axi_burst_splitter / id_fifo. The
// result is a model-wide input-combinational (ICO) settle blow-up that wedges
// the Verilator runtime.
//
// The SEP cocotb env only drives the tb top sep_uvm_top (root handle + its top-level
// ports: clocks/reset/boot controls + the flat s_axi_* bus). The CPU-LSU splice is
// SV-side inside the tb (the no_cpu stub drives lsu_axi_req from lsu_req_drive; the
// LSU response is read back by hierarchical name), not a cocotb VPI access. So cocotb
// needs public exposure of sep_uvm_top ONLY -- not the DUT fabric internals.
//
// Scoping public_flat_rw to sep_uvm_top (instead of the whole design) lets the fabric
// split_var pragmas activate again, and the model runs instead of wedging. No
// DUT/fabric RTL change is required.
//
// This file must be paired with dropping the runner's global --public-flat-rw (see
// the repo-controlled cocotb runner wrapper in the SEP DV flow).
public_flat_rw -module "sep_uvm_top" -var "*"

// The shared AXI VIP interface on the SEP->SMC boundary (rom_boot target):
// cocotb binds the slave agent to its members.
public_flat_rw -module "ocah_axi_if" -var "*"

// sep_wrapper DUT: tb_backdoor_mem in sep_uvm_top writes the real
// memory macro arrays (default-fill patterns + firmware/image loads). Those XMR writes
// no-op under Verilator unless the target array is public. These three cover all eight
// macros: prim_ram_1p.mem = SEP SRAM + KM SRAM (inner u_mem of prim_ram_1p_adv) + OTBN
// imem/dmem; prim_rom.mem = boot ROM + KM ROM; ram_16384x39.ram_core = ICCM (4 banks) +
// DCCM (2 banks) inside sep_tcm_wrapper. These arrays sit outside the hot AXI
// ready/valid cones, so exposing them does not re-arm the ICO blow-up.
public_flat_rw -module "prim_ram_1p"  -var "mem"
public_flat_rw -module "prim_rom"     -var "mem"
public_flat_rw -module "ram_16384x39" -var "ram_core"

// +sep_cold_scratch7 deposits the warm-handler address into
// sep_scratch_reg.field_storage before the CPU fetches. The CPU owns the
// system-CSR AXI frontdoor during firmware boot, so the testbench has no
// independent path for this timed write. The XMR deposit requires public write
// access to the leaf register storage, which sits outside the fabric AXI
// ready/valid combinational cones.
public_flat_rw -module "sep_scratch_reg" -var "field_storage"

// Do not add abr_wrapper_key_reg to this public list. The PeakRDL block is on
// the Bender filelist and tests reach it frontdoor. Also, no comment line here
// may START with the word "verilator" -- the .vlt lexer treats
// "// verilator ..." as a metacomment directive and errors out.
